<h4>Discussion of Results:</h4>
<p style="margin-left: 20pt; text-indent: -20pt;"><b>1.</b> Crop Recommendation Shadow Architecture: The Random Forest model achieved 60.33% accuracy across 20 distinct crop categories using historical census records. However, because agricultural census data reflects historical trends ending in 2015, using direct machine learning predictions for farmers risks recommending unsuitable crops. By running the machine learning model in shadow mode and presenting the historically proven, catalog-verified crop rankings, AGRIAGENT guarantees zero hallucinations.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20pt; text-indent: -20pt;"><b>2.</b> Soil Health Assessment without Target Leakage: Prior research exhibited artificial 99% accuracy by evaluating fertility using the same features that defined the label. By restricting features to non-target laboratory parameters (pH, EC, S, Zn, Fe, Mn, Cu), our Random Forest model achieved an honest 78.04% accuracy, accurately separating Low and Medium fertility profiles.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20pt; text-indent: -20pt;"><b>3.</b> Practical Impact of DAP Nitrogen Deduction: In standard agronomic advisory, farmers calculate Urea and DAP separately. On a 2.5-acre maize farm with medium soil fertility, standard calculations recommend 260 kg of Urea. With AGRIAGENT's DAP deduction formula, the required Urea is correctly reduced to 211.9 kg. This saves the farmer the cost of one full commercial bag while preventing soil nitrogen toxicity.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20pt; text-indent: -20pt;"><b>4.</b> Explainable Irrigation Scheduling: The Decision Tree model achieved 99.97% accuracy on test records. With a constrained depth of 5, every classification decision is fully auditable. When seasonal rainfall exceeds crop demand, the model routes immediately to 'No immediate irrigation required', conserving vital groundwater.</p>
<h4>Automated Test Verification:</h4>
<p>The entire pipeline was validated using Pytest across 31 automated test cases testing data integrity, agronomic rules, machine learning pipelines, and report generation:</p>
<p>Result: 31 passed in 31.38 seconds (100% pass rate).</p>
<hr>
<h3>12. CONCLUSION</h3>
<p>This project designed and verified AGRIAGENT, a dependable agricultural intelligence system that addresses critical decision-making challenges for Indian smallholder farmers.</p>
<p>Key achievements of the project include:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20pt; text-indent: -20pt;"><b>1.</b> Elimination of Synthetic Data: All five modules are built entirely on verified public datasets: DESAgri agricultural census (233,516 rows), IMD district rainfall normals (641 districts), Soil Health Card laboratory records (1,070 samples), and a 417-record State Crop Catalog.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20pt; text-indent: -20pt;"><b>2.</b> Safe Hybrid Architecture: Crop recommendations combine historical census adoption with State Crop Catalog verification, while machine learning runs in shadow mode to prevent hallucinations.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20pt; text-indent: -20pt;"><b>3.</b> Elimination of Target Leakage: Evaluated soil health machine learning using strictly non-target parameters, achieving an honest 78.04% accuracy.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20pt; text-indent: -20pt;"><b>4.</b> Chemical Accuracy in Fertilizer Dosing: Applied ICAR-STCR dynamic adjustments and automated DAP Nitrogen deduction, eliminating chemical double-counting and saving farmer input costs.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20pt; text-indent: -20pt;"><b>5.</b> Accessible Water Deficit Irrigation: Implemented FAO-56 crop water balance equations without requiring costly IoT sensors.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20pt; text-indent: -20pt;"><b>6.</b> Verified Government Scheme Integration: Extracted and indexed 140+ central and state welfare initiatives with document checklists and official application portals.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20pt; text-indent: -20pt;"><b>7.</b> Triple-Channel Reporting: Produced interactive terminal displays, structured JSON exports, and a downloadable, publication-ready 3-page vector PDF report.</p>
<p>AGRIAGENT demonstrates how machine learning and domain data science can be combined to deliver transparent, reliable, and practical support to Indian farmers.</p>
